<title>USA: US Treasury's 3-, 6-mo bills seen at 4.99/5.04 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury's 3-, 6-mo bills seen at 4.99/5.04 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's sale of $28.0 billion in three- and six-month bills is likely to produce average rates of 4.99 percent and 5.04 percent, respectively, traders said.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the auction is 1300 EST/1800 GMT.</p>
<p>In when-issued trade at around 1248 EST/1748 GMT, three-month bill rates were trading at 4.985 percent and six-month rates traded at 5.04 percent.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1679</p>
